NPC: mr_whitehouse
LOCATION: upper_residential_ridge
SCHEDULE: morning=bank_walk, midday=business_district, evening=home, night=home

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(mr_whitehouse, default)
  TAG: whitehouse_default
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  MR. WHITEHOUSE: "Corwin."
  [Mr. Whitehouse folds a newspaper against his cane with slow, practiced precision.]
  VOICE: trombone_alarmed_medium_v2
  MR. WHITEHOUSE: "If this is about the dead men, I advise you to distinguish inconvenience from catastrophe while the town still can."

TOPIC: subscriptions_and_credit
  GATE: always
  TAG: whitehouse_credit
  LABEL: "Ask why everyone keeps calling it arithmetic"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Every man I speak to gives me a different version of the same excuse."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. WHITEHOUSE: "Then you are hearing the truth from several angles at once."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Truth."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_long_v2
  MR. WHITEHOUSE: "Yes. Mills extend credit. Papers carry advertisers. Banks calm depositors. Houses keep staff employed. Remove confidence from a town this size and the rest follows it into the water."
  NOTEBOOK: whitehouse_confidence | "Whitehouse described the town's silence as a defense of confidence: banks, papers, houses, and wages depend on keeping panic out of print."
  EVIDENCE: civic_arithmetic

TOPIC: name_the_dead
  GATE: evidence(civic_arithmetic)
  TAG: whitehouse_dead
  LABEL: "Ask whether confidence matters more than the dead"
  TIME: 6
  FORK:
    CHOICE: "Say that eight people died, not six."
      VOICE: trombone_questioning_short_v1
      MR. WHITEHOUSE: "And if you print eight, do they revive?"
      VOICE: trombone_dismissive_long_v1
      MR. WHITEHOUSE: "No. But the bank run becomes real, the paper goes under, and every laundress and porter paid from those accounts discovers that your honesty has a payroll attached to it."
      NOTEBOOK: whitehouse_eight_payroll | "Whitehouse argued that acknowledging all eight dead would trigger wider economic harm the town's laboring people would bear."
    CHOICE: "Say that silence is still a choice."
      VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v2
      MR. WHITEHOUSE: "Of course it is."
      [He taps the folded newspaper once against his glove.]
      VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v2
      MR. WHITEHOUSE: "Adulthood consists largely of choosing which damage will be entered into the record and which will merely be survived."
      NOTEBOOK: whitehouse_silence_choice | "Whitehouse openly described public silence as a deliberate civic choice, not an accident."
      EVIDENCE: silence_is_choice